data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":235,"item_id":"fc_02f8293d92061092016adb4c419fe881918fef335c0bfec148","output_index":4,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"TASK_INCOMPLETE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"final interface authoring\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Resolved the previous apparent `AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor` issue: placing the map term directly in the type-probe list caused a term/type-category error. Defining a noncomputable wrapper with declared type `K ⊗[ℤ] M →ₗ[K] K ⊗[ℤ] M` compiles successfully. Thus the induced K-linear action on the swapped tensor view is available. I have still not completed source H004, exact conversion plan, or JSON artifact submission.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Latest check_lean_types passed the wrapper `act` whose body is `TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.lTensor K K f`; output confirms it returns the K-linear map on `K ⊗[ℤ] M`.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"The tensor action issue has a working typed implementation. Remaining work is complete source data/H004 encoding, prove/export tensor-commutor conversion, build all source-aligned S001-S008 obligations, and submit the artifact. No mathematical gap identified.\\\"}\"}"}

